    {
      "id": "instructions",
      "name": "Read before enabling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nRecord Olive Young Global bestseller prices and ranks in a Google Sheet. Run manually or once a day at 09:00 UTC. The workflow starts an Apify Actor, waits for it to finish, rejects incomplete output, then saves rows by a stable key. Repeating a sheet write for the same run updates those rows.\n\nThe first run sets the comparison baseline. Later runs compare the same ranking. This covers Global listing prices, not Korean-store prices or sales volume.\n\n### Setup\n1. Use your own Apify, n8n and Google Sheets accounts. Create a sheet tab with the [supplied headers](https://github.com/CRNO22/apify-workflow-examples/blob/main/samples/oliveyoung-sheet-headers.csv).\n2. Fill in Settings: spreadsheet ID, tab and a unique history-store name. Keep maxItems at 100 for a complete ranking.\n3. Select an Apify Header Auth credential on all four HTTP nodes: Authorization = Bearer YOUR_TOKEN. Connect Google Sheets OAuth.\n4. Run manually and inspect the saved rows before enabling the schedule. 100 saved rows cost $0.20; the default cap is $0.25. Other account charges may apply.\n\n### Customization\nChange the schedule to suit your reporting cycle. If a sheet write fails, recover that run’s saved dataset before collecting again. [Setup and recovery](https://github.com/CRNO22/apify-workflow-examples/blob/main/docs/oliveyoung-to-sheets.md).",
        "width": 680,
        "height": 660,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
